    "result_text": "The build passes and the test is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` as a read-only, human-formatted rendering of the owner's stored E.164 telephone, leaving raw `telephone` untouched.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` string property to the `Owner` schema (the DTOs are generated from this spec), documenting the format and that `telephone` stays E.164.\n\n2. **`TelephoneNormalizer.java`** \u2014 Added `toDisplay(String e164)`, which strips to digits, splits off the country code (recognising `+61` \u2192 2 digits and `+1` \u2192 1 digit, defaulting to 2), and joins the country code with the national digits grouped in threes: `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. Returns `null` for null/empty input.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired a `formatTelephoneDisplay` MapStruct qualifier (matching the existing derived-field pattern like `formatDisplayName`) that delegates to `TelephoneNormalizer.toDisplay(owner.getTelephone())`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` now passes: `$.telephone` = `+61412345678`, `$.telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`. Full suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
